{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.idempotent_of_sqrt_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.idempotent_of_sqrt_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L196-L215","doc":"**The CRT correction.**  If `R` *already* contains a square root `u` of `−1`\nand `2` is invertible, then any `R`-algebra containing an `x` with `x² = −1`\ncarries the nontrivial idempotent `e = 2⁻¹(1 + u·x)`.\n\nThis is the whole content of the splitting `R[X]/(X²+1) ≅ R × R`, and it is why\n`categorical-coordinate-ring-proof.md` rows 1 and 3 — which state\n`ℂ[i]/(i²+1) ≅ ℂ` — assert a non-isomorphism: `ℂ` is a field and has no\nidempotent other than `0` and `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_sq_eq_lambdaMinus_at_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_sq_eq_lambdaMinus_at_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L188-L194","doc":"The braiding link, recorded as arithmetic and nothing more.  At `q = 1` the\nantisymmetric braiding eigenvalue is `λ₋ = −q⁻¹ = −1`\n(`prop:braiding-eigenvalue-extraction`), so `J² = λ₋ · 1`: `J` is the square root\nof the antisymmetric eigenvalue the block extracts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.sq_eq_neg_one_iff_traceFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.sq_eq_neg_one_iff_traceFree","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L155-L186","doc":"The converse on the volume-form subgroup: within `det = 1`, squaring to `−1`\nis **equivalent** to trace-freeness.  So trace-freeness is not an extra choice\nmade to reach `i² = −1`; it is what squaring to `−1` means there.\n\nNo further hypothesis is needed — in particular no assumption that `2` is a\nnon-zero-divisor.  The determinant does the cancelling: `tr f • f = 0` kills\nevery entry, hence kills `tr f · det f`, and `det f = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.one_J_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.one_J_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L144-L153","doc":"**`R[i]` is a genuine extension, not a collapsed copy of `R`.**  `{1, J}` is\n`R`-linearly independent, so `R·1 ⊕ R·J ⊆ End(V)` is free of rank 2 — which is\nwhat upgrades \"a square root of `−1` exists\" to \"`R[i]` embeds\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_sq","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L138-L142","doc":"**Existence, so the forcing is not vacuous.**  `J² = −1`, obtained from the\ntheorem above rather than by a separate computation — the point being that `J`\nis not special: *any* trace-free `det`-one endomorphism would do. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_det","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L135-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J_trace","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L132-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.J","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L128-L130","doc":"The canonical quarter-turn.  `rem:affine-chart-origin-of-i-and-q` calls it\n`ρ_{π/2} = i·id_V`, the square root of the chart-swap involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.sq_eq_neg_one_of_traceFree_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.sq_eq_neg_one_of_traceFree_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L116-L126","doc":"**The forcing.**  On the subgroup the volume form selects — `det = 1`, i.e.\n`SL(V) = Sp(V)`, which `def:fundamental-object` says the volume form picks out\nover `GL₂` — every trace-free endomorphism squares to `−1`.\n\nNo square root is assumed anywhere: `i² = −1` is Cayley–Hamilton read on the\ntrace-free part of the group the volume form already gives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.sq_eq_trace_smul_sub_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.CategoricalCoordinateForced.sq_eq_trace_smul_sub_det","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumUniverse/CategoricalCoordinateForced.lean#L104-L114","doc":"**Cayley–Hamilton at rank two.**  `f² = (tr f)·f − (det f)·1`.\n\nThis is the whole mechanism: `det` is the scalar by which `Λ²f` acts on\n`Λ²V ≅ 𝟙`, so the volume form is exactly what makes the second coefficient\navailable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}